.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
backend.hcl
*.tfvars.json

# account.auto.tfvars holds the Cloudflare account id. It is not a secret, but it is not public in
# this repository either, so it is REQUIRED (no default) and supplied at apply time — never committed.
account.auto.tfvars

# terraform.tfvars is committed HERE on purpose, overriding `**/terraform.tfvars` in
# infra/.gitignore (and `infra/**/terraform.tfvars` in the root one) — the negation has to live in
# this file because it is deeper than both. Every value in it is public: the hostname IS the issuer
# every cloud trusts. See README.md.
!terraform.tfvars
